      "rationale": "A sanity check: does pendulum_lab period of ~1.67 beats (baseline) match known materials and geometry? Does resonator_obs frequency of ~4.06 cycles/beat align with expected circuit design? If either measurement is fundamentally miscalibrated, systematically offset from true units, or derived from the other through an undocumented transformation, the correlation patterns become uninterpretable. For example, if resonator_obs is computed as a function of pendulum_lab with a 3-day moving average or low-pass filter applied, the r=0.967 would be spurious. This is subsumable under 'hidden systematic error' (hypothesis 1) but warrants explicit mention given the precision-measurement goal. I should verify that both instruments were independently calibrated against known standards (e.g., atomic clock, precision frequency generator) and that no post-processing (windowing, smoothing, detrending) was applied selectively to one channel.",
